  "about": "One turn as the driver reads it. Codex records the turn's start before it announces the turn, so those records wait for it. The prompt Mako drew is not drawn again. Reasoning in two summary parts streams under its item's id and its record replaces the stream. A failing command's row is its call's record; its output streams onto it and its item finishes it, with the command's effects. An edit's row is its call's record, finished by its item with the patch it applied. The streamed answer gives way to its record and a late delta is dropped. Usage and a title come from the app-server, and the turn ends with its record.",
